摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"DSH browser tab favicon reflecting session state: idle / running / asking / done. · DSH 标签页 favicon 实时反映会话状态：待机 / 运行中 / 提问 / 完成","id":"gh:1339300677","install_available":true,"language":"JavaScript","name":"dsh-web-icon-indicator","slug":"waknow/dsh-web-icon-indicator","topics":["deepseek","deepseek-harness","dsh","dsh-plugin","favicon"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"DSH browser tab favicon reflecting session state: idle / running / asking / done. · DSH 标签页 favicon "},{"id":"p1s2","text":"实时反映会话状态：待机 / 运行中 / 提问 / 完成"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-web-icon-indicator"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"> 📖 中文文档 · English · 📝 Changelog · Releases · 🎨 Live demo"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"> **⚠️ DSH version support** — requires **DSH ≥ 0.1.2-rc.1**. One bundle serves both settings genera"},{"id":"p4s2","text":"tions: **modern** (≥ 0.1.7-alpha.1: exported `Config` schema + `configForms` + `plugins.bundle.confi"},{"id":"p4s3","text":"g`) and **legacy** (≤ 0.1.6-alpha.1: `settings.installSection` + `settingsScope` + `settings.plugin."},{"id":"p4s4","text":"item`). Verified on **DSH 0.1.5-rc.3** and **DSH 0.1.7-alpha.1**; on any older host the favicon stil"},{"id":"p4s5","text":"l works even if the settings page is not reachable."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"Browser tab favicon reflects the current DSH session state — `idle` / `running` / `asking` / `done` "},{"id":"p5s2","text":"— so you can see at a glance whether a session needs your attention, even when the tab is in the bac"},{"id":"p5s3","text":" can see at a glance whether a session needs your attention, even when the tab is in the background."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"> 🎨 **Live demo** — <https://waknow.github.io/dsh-web-icon-indicator/> · see the four states, the mu"},{"id":"p6s2","text":"lti-agent counter and every effect rendered live in your browser, no install needed. The playground "},{"id":"p6s3","text":"even drives the demo page's own tab favicon, exactly like the plugin does on a DSH page."},{"id":"p7s1","text":"## ✨ What it does"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"- **Live session state on the tab favicon** — the browser-tab icon mirrors `idle` / `running` / `ask"},{"id":"p8s2","text":"ing` / `done` (aggregate priority: `asking` > `running` > `done` > `idle`), so background tabs tell "},{"id":"p8s3","text":"you at a glance what your agents are doing — including `ask_user_question` prompts and approval / sa"},{"id":"p8s4","text":"ndbox-escalation waits, which pin the icon to `asking`.\n- **One SVG, recolored & animated in the bro"},{"id":"p8s5","text":"wser** — ships a single whale template (`icons/base.svg`); every state, color and frame is rendered "},{"id":"p8s6","text":"client-side as a `data:image/svg+xml` URI. No per-color icon files.\n- **Six built-in effects** — `st"},{"id":"p8s7","text":"atic`, `blink`, `breath`, `rainbow`, `heartbeat`, `bounce` — all driven by JavaScript, since favicon"},{"id":"p8s8","text":"s don't play SVG CSS animations.\n- **Fully configurable, applied live** — every state's color, effec"},{"id":"p8s9","text":"t and cycle speed, plus the asking/done hold timings, apply to the running tab within ~1 s — no relo"},{"id":"p8s10","text":"ad, no restart.\n- **Built-in settings UI, zero YAML** — the *Favicon indicator* page edits the whole"},{"id":"p8s11","text":" config with live color-swatch previews and persists it for you (modern hosts: the profile patch; le"},{"id":"p8s12","text":"gacy hosts: the profile `settings.yaml` — paths below).\n- **Background-tab & restart-proof** — anima"},{"id":"p8s13","text":"ted states keep a wall-clock fallback while `requestAnimationFrame` is paused in hidden tabs, and th"},{"id":"p8s14","text":"e status poll self-heals across host restarts. Returning to a tab repaints immediately: a `visibilit"},{"id":"p8s15","text":"ychange` listener fires an instant status fetch, so a state that flipped while the tab was hidden (e"},{"id":"p8s16","text":".g. the `done` hold expiring) shows at once instead of waiting for the next — possibly throttled — p"},{"id":"p8s17","text":"oll tick. When the backend is stopped, the tab never loses its icon: the outage restores the shell's"},{"id":"p8s18","text":" own favicon from an offline-safe `data:`-URI copy (or keeps the last painted frame), and the live i"},{"id":"p8s19","text":"con returns on the first successful poll.\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"### 🛠 Configuration UI — how to get there"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"| # | Step |"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"| 1 | Open the DSH Web GUI and go to **Settings / 设置** → **Plugins / 插件**. |\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"## How it works"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"## Browser support & known limitations"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"The favicon is a plain image, so browsers never run the SVG's own CSS/JS animation inside the tab UI"},{"id":"p15s2","text":" — every frame is rendered here in JavaScript. How well a *changing* favicon is displayed differs by"},{"id":"p15s3","text":"frame is rendered here in JavaScript. How well a *changing* favicon is displayed differs by browser:"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"| Browser | SVG favicon | Live per-state color/effect | Why |"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"| Chrome / Edge | ✅ | ✅ smooth | Re-reads `<link rel=icon>` live; `data:`-URI SVGs are fine. |\n| Fir"},{"id":"p17s2","text":"efox | ✅ | ✅ smooth | Renders SVG favicons well (and honors their `prefers-color-scheme`, unused her"},{"id":"p17s3","text":"e). |\n| Safari (macOS) | ✅ rendered static | ⚠️ best-effort | Ignores in-SVG CSS; aggressive icon ca"},{"id":"p17s4","text":"ching. |\n| Safari (iOS) | ✅ rendered static | ⚠️ rarely | Unlikely to refresh without revisiting the"},{"id":"p17s5","text":"|\n| Safari (iOS) | ✅ rendered static | ⚠️ rarely | Unlikely to refresh without revisiting the tab. |"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"Known limitations (current as of Safari 26.3):"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"- **Favicons have their own cache.** Chrome keeps a favicon database, Firefox a `favicons.sqlite`, a"},{"id":"p19s2","text":"nd **Safari a system-level icon cache** — none of which a normal *clear cache* touches, and WebKit e"},{"id":"p19s3","text":"ven caches the \"no icon\" case. That is why a changed icon can linger for an existing tab. The plugin"},{"id":"p19s4","text":" already mitigates this: it serves `base.svg` and the status endpoint with `Cache-Control: no-store`"},{"id":"p19s5","text":", bundles a freshness query (`?t=Date.now()`) on its fetches, and replaces the `<link rel=icon>` nod"},{"id":"p19s6","text":"e on each state change.\n- **A theme-scoped favicon pair must be collapsed first (DSH ≥ 0.1.7).** The"},{"id":"p19s7","text":" shell's `index.html` ships *two* `rel=icon` links — `favicon-dark.svg` for `prefers-color-scheme: d"},{"id":"p19s8","text":"ark` and `favicon.svg` for light — because up to `0.1.6-alpha.2` there was exactly one. A browser re"},{"id":"p19s9","text":"solves the favicon to the **last connected link whose `media` matches**, so repainting only the firs"},{"id":"p19s10","text":"t one left the tab showing the shell's icon no matter what the session did. The plugin now normalize"},{"id":"p19s11","text":"s the set to a single always-matching link at startup (keeping the variant your scheme selects) befo"},{"id":"p19s12","text":"re painting. If you are on a version before 0.5.2 and the tab icon simply never changes, this is why"},{"id":"p19s13","text":"g. If you are on a version before 0.5.2 and the tab icon simply never changes, this is why.\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"## Caveats"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"- Favicon SVG CSS animations do not run inside the browser's tab UI — all effects are produced in Ja"},{"id":"p21s2","text":"vaScript by rebuilding the data-URI each frame. This is a deliberate, zero-dependency design. (The a"},{"id":"p21s3","text":"nimated previews in this README are demo assets for illustration only — the favicon itself is JS-ani"},{"id":"p21s4","text":"mated.)\n- Favicon behavior differs by browser, and Safari is the most limited — see Browser support "},{"id":"p21s5","text":"& known limitations.\n- The base template must keep its `__COLOR__` placeholder in the `#p { fill: … "},{"id":"p21s6","text":"}` rule; the browser replaces that token to color each frame.\n- The plugin runs in the **host** plan"},{"id":"p21s7","text":"e; it must be mounted into a profile's composition, not a session-scoped agent preset.\n- File reads "},{"id":"p21s8","text":"go through the `fs` service with the configured `iconsDir` as `cwd`. Make sure that path is readable"},{"id":"p21s9","text":" under your deployment's sandbox policy."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
